        "subject": "LU-20882 scripts: fix man page version lookup under dash",
        "message": "LU-20882 scripts: fix man page version lookup under dash\n\ncheckpatch-man.pl looks up the release that added a man\npage's subject by running a git log/awk pipeline through\nPerl backticks, which use /bin/sh. The pipeline fed git log\nto awk with a bash here-string (<<<). On Debian and Ubuntu\n/bin/sh is dash, which rejects that with \"Syntax error:\nredirection unexpected\", so the AVAILABILITY lookup never\nran there and always reported \"no git commit hash found\".\n\nPipe the git log output into awk instead, grouped in a\nsubshell since it can be an \"a || b\" list, and take the\n10-character short hash with substr() rather than another\nhere-string through head.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: d15955d374d5 (\"LU-4315 doc: add man pages to checkpatch\")\nAssisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.1-sol\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ice0101ada39ced39c2e5967649cf6ae9ede694c2\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69460\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
